login: root

root@OSB A:\OSB\ROOT>

root@OSB A:\OSB\ROOT>HELP
OSB shell commands:
  VER HELP CLS CLEAR MEM REBOOT
  TIME DATE TICKS SLEEP ECHO SET DIR CD PWD TYPE SIZE MD RD
  DEL REN MOVE COPY CP SIZE LN
  TRASH USER LOGIN LOGOUT WHOAMI
  CHOWN CHMOD SUDO HISTORY TASK PS KILL WAIT TAB SPAWN
  EXIT LOGOUT
Detail:   COMMAND /?        shows the help page of one command
Files:    DIR [path] [/W]  CD [path]  PWD  TYPE <file>  (ext4/A:)
          MD  RD  DEL (to trash)  REN/MOVE  COPY  SIZE  LN [/S]  COLOR  CLEAR/CLS
          TRASH [/F <pattern>]  list/search the per-user trash ($HOME\TRASH)
          TRASH /U <name>       undelete back to the original folder
History:  HISTORY [n]     numbered list (100 latest by default)
          (:N)            re-run entry N of the history
          Up/Down         walk the history while editing
Editing:  TAB completes commands, /flags and filenames
Users:    USER            list accounts (uid 0 = root)
          USER /ADD <name> [password]   /CHANGE  /DEL <name> [/HOME]
          USER /SUDO <name> | /UNSUDO <name>  edit the sudoers
          LOGIN [name]    switch user (passwordless for root)
          EXIT | LOGOUT   end the session, back to 'login:'
Perms:    CHOWN <user> <path>   CHMOD <octal> <path>  (root/owner)
          A:\OSB is root-owned; HOME folders are the user's;
          A:\OSB\CONF holds PASSWD and SUDOERS; SUDO runs as root
Processes:SPAWN [BAD|SPAWNER] [&]  start a ring-3 process
          RING3 [BAD] [&]  synonym for SPAWN
          TASK / PS        list processes (a simple ps)
          KILL <pid>       terminate a process
          WAIT <pid>       wait for a child and collect its code
          TAB <pid>        bring a process to the foreground
          Add '&' to run in the background; Ctrl+C aborts a
          foreground job and returns to the shell.
root@OSB A:\OSB\ROOT>
root@OSB A:\OSB\ROOT>
